<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mzimvubu River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Umzimvubu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mzimvubu is one of the largest rivers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-cape">Eastern Cape</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, rising in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drakensberg">Drakensberg</a> and reaching the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-st-johns">Port St Johns</a>. Its upper valleys were the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpondomise">Mpondomise</a>, and its lower course ran through Pondoland. It is one of the few large South African rivers without a major dam.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mzimvubu-river.jpg" alt="Mzimvubu River" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IY188_pg018_THE_MOUTH_OF_THE_UMZIMVUBU_%27GATES%27_OF_ST_JOHN%27S_RIVER,_NATAL.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
